aining Shea in a place  like this he is learning you know  socialization skills interacting with  the crowd interacting with the players  on the field and ultimately that'll help  make him a better service dog he is  absolutely my best friend Air Force  veteran Nathan Gardner got Kenzo in  February it's been life-changing knowing  that I'm not alone anymore and taking me  out of that Despair and getting me  strength and helping me find myself  again good boy Shea will continue with  the Mets through spring training next  year he could change someone's life he  will change somebody's life steady a  winning Play All Around good boy Nancy  Chen CBS News New York  it's a good boy all right our next and  final story is about a teenage boy who  heard about a family in his neighborhood  a family that needed a boost in a big  way and he came up with a very creative  way to help them here's Caitlin O'Kane  again with his story  when hurricane Ida hit Louisiana last  year the Estevez family's home was  destroyed as they began to rebuild their  lives they were gutted again their  nine-month-old daughter Blakely had  cancer  I mean it was the worst news we we could  ever hear obviously hearing your child  has cancer is not easy and it's just  like almost like what else can go wrong  you know it's just another thing  happening  need of a home the Estevez has moved  into a family member's house on their  new Street lived a high school swimmer  named Drew Lonnie  Drew heard about the new family in his  neighborhood displaced by a hurricane  and he learned that their baby had  cancer he was compelled to help so I  decided to swim for Blakely doing the  thing that I know how to do Drew and his  teammates from Holy Cross High School  held a lapse for Blakely event raising  money by having members of the community  sponsor each swimmer we both were in a  grandson like the Young Generation has  hope after all his kids doing this all  on his own and uh I know I said I'll be  there no ma